{
  "sn42.2:0.1": "Linked Discourses 42.2 ",
  "sn42.2:0.2": "1. Chiefs ",
  "sn42.2:0.3": "With Tālapuṭa ",
  "sn42.2:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the squirrels’ feeding ground. ",
  "sn42.2:1.2": "Then Tālapuṭa the dancing chief came up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him: ",
  "sn42.2:1.3": "“Sir, I have heard that the dancers of the past who were tutors of tutors said: ",
  "sn42.2:1.4": "‘Suppose a dancer entertains and amuses people on a stage or at a festival with mixed truth and lies. When their body breaks up, after death, they’re reborn in the company of laughing gods.’ ",
  "sn42.2:1.5": "What does the Buddha say about this?” ",
  "sn42.2:1.6": "“Enough, chief, let it be. Don’t ask me that.” ",
  "sn42.2:1.7": "For a second time … ",
  "sn42.2:1.8": "",
  "sn42.2:1.9": "",
  "sn42.2:1.10": "",
  "sn42.2:1.11": "",
  "sn42.2:1.12": "And for a third time Tālapuṭa said to the Buddha: ",
  "sn42.2:1.13": "“Sir, I have heard that the dancers of the past who were tutors of tutors said: ",
  "sn42.2:1.14": "‘Suppose a dancer entertains and amuses people on a stage or at a festival with mixed truth and lies. When their body breaks up, after death, they’re reborn in the company of laughing gods.’ ",
  "sn42.2:1.15": "What does the Buddha say about this?” ",
  "sn42.2:2.1": "“Clearly, chief, I’m not getting through to you when I say: ",
  "sn42.2:2.2": "‘Enough, chief, let it be. ",
  "sn42.2:2